---
description: Hono API server conventions
globs: apps/server/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- Hono on `@hono/node-server`, run with `tsx`. No build step.
- Define routes by chaining on the `app` in `src/app.ts` (or chain
  sub-apps with `.route()`), so `AppType` keeps full types for the web
  `hc` client. Do not register routes in separate statements.
- Keep `src/app.ts` free of side effects so tests can call
  `app.request()`. Process setup (listen, signals) stays in `src/index.ts`.
- Validate params, query and JSON bodies with zod via
  `@hono/zod-validator` (add it when the first route needs it). Put
  request and response schemas in `packages/shared`.
- Return JSON with an explicit status: `c.json(body, 200)`.
- Websockets use `upgradeWebSocket` from `@hono/node-server` with the
  `ws` server passed to `serve`. Do not use `@hono/node-ws`.
- Listen on `127.0.0.1` only. Port from `PORT`, default 8787.
- Test routes with Vitest and `app.request()` in `src/*.test.ts`.
